{
  "source": "v2-baseline",
  "logic": "How a v2 receipt prints amounts (ReceiptFormats: hellers as Czech crowns with U+00A0 as the thousands separator and before Kč, hellers only when not whole; English as CZK with a comma and a point), dates (Czech d. M. yyyy without leading zeros, which the web's 15. 03. 2026 is not; English d MMMM yyyy) and the donor (ReceiptData from the donor record: trimmed name, identifier of a company, address as street, postal code city). input.format names the formatter; expected.text or expected.donor is what the receipt's frozen data holds",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "1 heller in Czech",
      "input": {
        "format": "czechAmount",
        "amountMinor": 1
      },
      "expected": {
        "text": "0,01 Kč"
      }
    },
